## Building

This tree targets TWRP's AOSP-based minimal manifest
([twrp-12.1 / twrp-14.1](https://github.com/minimal-manifest-twrp/platform_manifest_twrp_aosp)).

```bash
mkdir twrp && cd twrp
repo init --depth=1 -u https://github.com/minimal-manifest-twrp/platform_manifest_twrp_aosp.git -b twrp-12.1
repo sync -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags

# Place this tree in device/{{ device_info.manufacturer }}/{{ device_info.codename }}

. build/envsetup.sh
lunch twrp_{{ device_info.codename }}-eng
mka {{ "bootimage" if tree.recovery_as_boot else "recoveryimage" }}
```

The image will be in `out/target/product/{{ device_info.codename }}/{{ "boot.img" if tree.recovery_as_boot else "recovery.img" }}`.

On newer sources that require a release config, use `lunch twrp_{{ device_info.codename }}-ap2a-eng` (or the release name of your branch).

{% if tree.uses_dynamic_partitions and not tree.super_partition_size_is_known %}
## Before building

`BOARD_SUPER_PARTITION_SIZE` in `BoardConfig.mk` is a placeholder. Replace it with
the real size of your super partition (`adb shell blockdev --getsize64 /dev/block/by-name/super`).

{% endif %}
## Tree layout

```
{{ device_info.codename }}/
├── Android.bp / Android.mk
├── AndroidProducts.mk
├── BoardConfig.mk
├── device.mk
├── twrp_{{ device_info.codename }}.mk
├── vendorsetup.sh
├── recovery.fstab                    # mountable partitions (AOSP format)
├── prebuilt/                         # kernel, dtb, dtbo from the stock image
└── recovery/root/
    ├── *.rc                          # init scripts from the stock recovery
{% if tree.kernel_modules %}
    ├── lib/modules/                  # kernel modules ({{ tree.kernel_modules|length }}), loaded by TW_LOAD_VENDOR_MODULES
{% endif %}
    └── system/etc/twrp.flags         # raw partitions (backup/flash) and removable storage
```

{% if tree.is_samsung %}
## Samsung notes

TWRP can't decrypt Samsung's `/data`, so you'll need to format data after flashing.
To flash with Odin, pack the image as a tar: `tar -cvf twrp.tar {{ "boot.img" if tree.recovery_as_boot else "recovery.img" }}`.
Use **Advanced → Reboot → Download** to go back to Odin mode.

{% endif %}
{% if tree.uses_crypto %}
## Decryption

Encryption support is enabled in `BoardConfig.mk`, but decrypting `/data` also needs
the device's keymaster/keymint and gatekeeper blobs (and their dependencies) copied
into `recovery/root/vendor`.

{% endif %}
